     I may be wrong, but...
     Your 0-1 variables are also ordinal. Are they being treated as ordinal in the model? You should not need to change this, but I'm curious.
     Many of the variables in your model are being treated as exogenous by default, because they are not dependent on anything in your model. But when you declara covariances between some of them, you change the default treatment for those variables to endogenous. When treated as exogenous, their variances and covariances are not free model parameters but are simply taken from the data. Unless you want those variables treated as endogenous, I think you can remove the syntax specifying covariances. You also might add the option, "fixed.x = T" to make the exogeneity explicit.
I have never myself seen the lavaan message in your email--sorry.
--Ed Rigdon

